faqs:
  - q: "How does the Days Until Date Calculator work?"
    a: "The calculator compares your selected target date with the current date at local midnight in your device's timezone. It computes the difference in total days, converts those days into weeks and months, and identifies the day of the week."
  - q: "Does this calculator take leap years into account?"
    a: "Yes. The algorithm accounts for 366-day leap years (including February 29th) automatically when computing day differences across calendar years."
  - q: "Why might date calculations be off by one day on other websites?"
    a: "Other websites often use UTC timestamps or fail to adjust for time zone differences. ToolsBuilt performs all calculations strictly at local midnight in your browser timezone to prevent off-by-one errors."
  - q: "Can I calculate how many days have passed since a past date?"
    a: "Yes. If you select a date in the past, the calculator automatically detects it and displays the total days elapsed since that event."
  - q: "Is my input date stored or sent to a server?"
    a: "No. All calculation logic runs locally inside your browser using standard JavaScript. No personal dates or event names leave your device."
